• Therefore, 0.05 mol NaHCO₃ produces 0.05 mol CO₂.

Step 3. Calculate the volume of CO₂ at 273°C:
• First, convert 273°C to Kelvin:
  T = 273 + 273 = 546 K (approximately)

• Use the ideal gas law: V = (nRT)/P
  Assuming a pressure of 1 atm and using R = 0.08206 L·atm/(mol·K):
  V = (0.05 mol × 0.08206 L·atm/(mol·K) × 546 K) / 1 atm

• Compute the volume:
  V ≈ 0.05 × (0.08206 × 546)
  0.08206 × 546 ≈ 44.8
  V ≈ 0.05 × 44.8 = 2.24 L

Thus, the volume of CO₂ liberated is approximately 2.24 liters, which corresponds to Option E.
