To calculate the radiation resistance (R_rad), we use the formula:

  R_rad = P / I²

Where:
 P = Radiated power = 8000 W (8 kW)
 I = Current = 20 A

Plugging in the values:

  R_rad = 8000 W / (20 A)²
  R_rad = 8000 W / 400 A²
  R_rad = 20 ohms

Thus, the radiation resistance is 20 ohms, which corresponds to option H.
