We start by noting that in a DC shunt motor the field winding is connected directly across the supply so that its current (and hence flux) remains nearly constant. Thus, the speed is essentially proportional to the net armature voltage (back‐emf) which is given by

  Vₐ = V – (brush drop + IₐRₐ).

At full load the following data are given:
 • Supply voltage, V = 120 V
 • Armature resistance, Rₐ = 0.2 Ω
 • Field resistance, R_f = 60 Ω
 • Line current, I_line = 40 A
 • Brush voltage drop = 3 V
 • Full load speed = 1800 rpm

Step 1. Find the field current:
  I_f = V/R_f = 120/60 = 2 A

Step 2. Determine the full‐load armature current:
  Iₐ = I_line – I_f = 40 – 2 = 38 A

Step 3. Compute the armature voltage at full load:
  Vₐ(full load) = 120 – 3 – (38 × 0.2)
    = 120 – 3 – 7.6
    = 109.4 V

Since speed N ∝ Vₐ (with constant field flux), we have at full load:
  k · N_full = 109.4  or  k = 109.4/1800

Now, we calculate for the two different loading conditions.

───────────────────────────── 
(a) Half Load

At half load the line current is 20 A. The field current remains 2 A, so:
  Iₐ (half load) = 20 – 2 = 18 A

Now compute the armature voltage:
  Vₐ(half load) = 120 – 3 – (18 × 0.2)
    = 120 – 3 – 3.6
    = 113.4 V

Since speed is proportional to Vₐ:
  N(half load) = (Vₐ(half load)/Vₐ(full load)) × 1800
    = (113.4/109.4) × 1800
    ≈ 1.0371 × 1800 ≈ 1867 rpm

───────────────────────────── 
(b) Overload of 125%

At 125% overload the line current is:
  I_line = 1.25 × 40 = 50 A

The field current is still 2 A so:
  Iₐ (overload) = 50 – 2 = 48 A

Now compute the armature voltage:
  Vₐ(overload) = 120 – 3 – (48 × 0.2)
    = 120 – 3 – 9.6
    = 107.4 V

Thus, the speed at overload is:
  N(overload) = (107.4/109.4) × 1800
    ≈ 0.981 × 1800 ≈ 1766 rpm

───────────────────────────── 
Comparison with Options

Our calculated speeds are approximately:
 • Half load: 1867 rpm
 • 125% overload: 1766 rpm

Looking at the provided options, Option G states:
 • Half-load speed: 1860 rpm
 • 1(1/4) load speed: 1765 rpm

This is the closest match to our calculations.

───────────────────────────── 
Final Answer

Option G.
