  t = r·√[(n – 2)/(1 – r²)],

which under H₀ follows a t-distribution with n – 2 degrees of freedom. For a two‐tailed test at significance level α = 0.05, we reject H₀ if

  |t| > t₍α/2, n–2₎.

Here r = 0.68 and 1 – r² = 1 – 0.68² = 1 – 0.4624 = 0.5376.

