  Degrees of freedom = 7 – 2 = 5.
  t = 0.68·√[(7 – 2)/0.5376] = 0.68·√(5/0.5376) ≈ 0.68·√(9.3) ≈ 0.68·3.05 ≈ 2.08.
  The critical t-value for 5 df at the 0.975 quantile is approximately 2.57.
  Since 2.08 < 2.57, we do not reject H₀.

2. For n = 8:
  Degrees of freedom = 8 – 2 = 6.
  t = 0.68·√[(8 – 2)/0.5376] = 0.68·√(6/0.5376) ≈ 0.68·√(11.16) ≈ 0.68·3.34 ≈ 2.27.
