We analyze each statement:

Statement 1: "For any two groups G and G', there exists a homomorphism of G into G'."  
This is true because for any groups G and G', the trivial homomorphism defined by sending every element of G to the identity element of G' is a valid group homomorphism.

Statement 2: "Every homomorphism is a one-to-one map."  
This is false because a homomorphism is one-to-one (injective) if and only if its kernel is trivial. Many homomorphisms, such as the trivial homomorphism, have a nontrivial kernel and are therefore not one-to-one.

Thus, the correct answer is: D. True, False.
